spans.s:
pīṭhikā,
(1) base, pedestal (of a divine figure; cf. Skt. pīṭha): pṛthivī tasya pī˚ Kv 〔15.9〕 (misprinted pīthikā); this is the definition of pw, but perhaps footstool is at least equally probable;
(2) in Kv 〔32.18〕 perh. error for piṭakā or piṭikā = Skt. piṭaka, basket, in lit. sense (cf. pīṭhaka): pīṭhikām upagṛhya, said of Rāma (Viṣṇu) masquerading as a brahman dwarf in mendicantʼs garb; pīṭhikā surely means something which an ascetic might carry (hardly footstool!).
